🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- indexing a multi-dimensional struct array
🚽 field with the wrong number of indices must be rejected outright, not
🚽 silently truncated. calculate_array_offset()'s own dimension-mismatch
🚽 handling is a lenient "TEMPORARY FIX" (its own comment) that
🚽 truncates to whichever index count is smaller and keeps going -- fine
🚽 for a standalone array's own private buffer, not for a field living
🚽 inline in a struct's shared blob, where a silently-accepted rank
🚽 mismatch would compute an offset for the wrong number of dimensions
🚽 and read/write into a neighboring field's bytes instead. evaluate_
🚽 struct_field_array_access() (ast.c) checks rank itself before ever
🚽 calling calculate_array_offset(), so this never reaches that lenient
🚽 path at all.
gang Grid {
    rizz cells[2][3];
};

skibidi main {
    gang Grid g;
    g.cells[1] = 5;
}
